--- a/core/api/v2/doc.go
+++ b/core/api/v2/doc.go
@@ -8,34 +8,31 @@
 //
 //	@title							Anytype API v2
 //	@version						2025-11-08
-//	@description					The agent-oriented Anytype local API. An object is one AnyBlock JSON document rather than a tree of blocks, so a single GET returns a whole editable document and a single PATCH edits it.
-//	@description					Everything this API names for itself is snake_case: path and query parameters, request and response fields, and the names of the PATCH ops. Things are addressed by name rather than by id: property keys, option names, and `type` as a type key. Object ids remain ids.
-//	@description					Property and type keys have two spellings, and a served body picks one. The default is the key: a snake_case slug minted when the property was created and frozen from then on, so it survives every rename. Store that spelling in a config, a script, an integration. `?keys=name` on a read serves the display-name vocabulary instead, "Due date" rather than due_date, which is the spelling to show a user their own words. Input needs no such choice: every channel accepts both, plus the forgiving fold between them, so dueDate, due-date, "Due date" and Дата выполнения all address the property they name. A spelling matching two properties is a 400 listing both, and an unknown one never creates anything.
